    "body": "Follow-up to #42321.\r\n\r\nProblem:\r\nnews.txt does not list the '] change from #42321.\r\n\r\nSolution:\r\nAdd a news entry. The doc change is covered by vim-patch 9.2.1233 (#42536).\r\n\r\n<details><summary>Original description</summary>\r\n<!--\r\n  Thank you for contributing to Neovim!\r\n  If this is your first time, check out https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#pull-requests-prs\r\n  for our PR guidelines.\r\n-->\r\nFollow-up to #42321.\r\n\r\nProblem:\r\n`:h exclusive` does not cover a motion forced blockwise, and `:h o_CTRL-V` does not say if the motion's inclusive/exclusive type applies.\r\n\r\nSolution:\r\n- `:h o_CTRL-V`: the type does not apply. The block follows Visual block mode, align the built-in operators do.\r\n- `:h exclusive`: point to `:h o_CTRL-V`.\r\n- `news.txt`: list the `']` change from #42321.\r\n</details>\r\n",
    "closed_at": null,
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "@echasnovski I found a counterexample tothe rule I wanted to add (\"Inclusive and exclusive do not apply to\r\n|o_CTRL-V|\"): ``d<C-v>`x`` uses the exclusive flag and deletes nothing.\r\n\r\nBy coincidence, you reported this in #24613. I plan to fix it first, and update doc with that fix. For now, this PR has only the news.txt entry. What do you think?",
